# Validation Rules

A template

* must have a unique name within the same DocumentType
* cannot have more than one default template for the same DocumentType
* cannot be deleted if it is the default
* cannot update non-existent email types

Use BusinessException for validation failures.

---

# Future Compatibility (Do Not Implement Yet)

Design the code so it can later support:

* HTML rendering
* PDF generation
* Email sending
* Variable replacement
* Multiple renderer strategies
* Version history
* Template preview
* Template cloning

Do not implement these yet.

---

# Important Architecture Rules

* Follow SOLID principles.
* Keep controllers thin.
* Put business rules in the service layer.
* Use transactions where necessary.
* Use mapper classes instead of exposing entities.
* Use DTOs for all requests and responses.
* Use cascading only where appropriate.
* The module must be reusable by future document types (Invoices, Quotes, Purchase Orders, Credit Notes, Receipts, Delivery Notes).
* Do not couple this module to the Invoice module.

